      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waverly%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1853, the borough was renamed Waverly after Sir Walter Scott's novel, since another Abington existed near Philadelphia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.waverlytwp.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the mid‑19th century, Waverly served as a stop on the Underground Railroad.",
